<Layout
  title="Claude Sonnet 5 — A.I. — Rycode"
  description="Speed-and-intelligence balance for everyday coding and agents."
  variant="ai"
>
  <article class="ai-model">
    <p class="ai-model-kicker">Frontier models</p>
    <h1 class="ai-model-title">Claude Sonnet 5</h1>
    <p class="ai-model-dek">Claude Sonnet 5 is Anthropic’s speed-and-intelligence balance model for everyday coding and agents. The API id is <code>claude-sonnet-5</code>. Pricing is $2 input and $10 output per million tokens.</p>
    <hr class="ai-model-rule" />
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Training</h2>
    <p>Anthropic lists a reliable knowledge and training data cutoff of January 2026. Parameter count, training FLOPs, and the full post-training recipe for this SKU are not published on the models overview or choosing guide.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Inference</h2>
    <p>Adaptive thinking is supported. Default effort is <code>high</code>. Relative to the current Claude lineup, Sonnet is the fast latency class.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Context</h2>
    <p>The documented context window is 1 million tokens. Max output is 128K tokens. Inputs are text and images; output is text. The model supports multilingual use, vision, and tool use.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Methods</h2>
    <p>Anthropic names an effort parameter and tools for this SKU.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Benchmarking</h2>
    <p>Anthropic has not published a Sonnet 5 score table on the models overview or the Fable announce pages cited here. The Fable announce table covers Fable and Opus columns, not Sonnet 5.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Hardware</h2>
    <p>Anthropic trains and runs Claude on AWS Trainium, Google TPUs, and NVIDIA GPUs. Amazon is the primary cloud and training partner. Anthropic reported more than 1 million Trainium2 chips in use as of April 2026. Per-SKU serving silicon is not published. Buyers purchase API tokens, not a named Claude GPU SKU.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Access and pricing</h2>
    <p>Pricing is $2 input and $10 output per million tokens.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Sources</h2>
    <ul class="ai-model-sources">
